# Grabby Giant: the sacrifice may be a land. On turn 3 Bot1 plays a Mountain, then pays {2}{R} with a Black Lotus and sacrifices
# that Mountain (an untapped land is fine, CR 118.3): the Mountain goes to the graveyard, a card is drawn (hand 3 after the land
# drop, 4 after the draw) and the Giant stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus x2
Mox Ruby
Grabby Giant
Mountain x3
Mountain x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Grabby Giant.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Grabby Giant.Activate
! Bot1.Choose(Grabby Giant)
Bot1.Choose(Mountain)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 4

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Mountain; Black Lotus; Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield = Grabby Giant; Mox Ruby
